description.narrative:
"1) Facilitating the generation of greenhouse gas emission reductions from small-scale projects which alleviate poverty and improve the quality of life of local communities in poorer countries and rural areas of the developing world.  To this aim, the Fund Management will use its best endeavors to place a minimum of 25 percent of the CDCF capital into eligible projects located in Least Developed Countries and other poor developing countries, where these are defined as (i) countries listed in the  Bank.s International Development Association (.IDA.) list of countries eligible to borrow from IDA; (ii) countries commonly referred to as .IDA blend. with a population of less than 75 million; or (iii) countries designated as Least Developed Countries (LDCs) by the United Nations.  The CDCF may also support small-scale projects in countries other than LDCs and other poor developing countries, provided these projects will provide direct independently certifiable benefits to the poorer and rural communities of those countries.
 2) Stimulating private capital flows for sustainable development in accordance with the Plan of Implementation concluded at the Johannesburg World Summit for Sustainable Development;
 3) Helping build a market for the emission reductions generated and expand the reach of carbon finance and the Clean Development Mechanism to developing countries which would otherwise be potentially excluded from the benefits of the emerging carbon market."
